iti96:5.1 starts: While those who’ve cut off doubt
iti96:5.2 starts: have no more conceit
iti96:5.3 starts: They who have reached
iti96:5.4 starts: while in the world
iti98:6.1 starts: Both for those who proclaim it
iti98:6.2 starts: and those who listen,
iti98:6.3 starts: confident in the message of the One
iti98:6.4 starts: it purifies their foremost benefit–
iti100:7.1 starts: He who, unstinting,
iti100:7.2 starts: the Tathāgata,
iti100:7.3 starts: to one of that sort
iti100:7.4 starts: to one gone
iti102:4.1 starts: then, the gnosis of one released–
iti102:4.2 starts: release-knowledge, superlative,
iti102:4.3 starts: the knowledge of ending:
iti102:4.4 starts: ‘The fetters are ended.’
iti104:3.1 starts: This is a condition
iti104:3.2 starts: for those who know:
iti104:3.3 starts: living the Dhamma
iti104:3.4 starts: composed in mind.
iti106:4.1 starts: Mother & father,
iti106:4.2 starts: first teachers,
iti106:4.3 starts: those worthy of gifts
iti106:4.4 starts: from their children.
iti106:6.1 starts: Performing these services to their parents,
iti106:6.2 starts: the wise
iti106:6.3 starts: are praised right here
iti106:6.4 starts: and after death
iti107:4.1 starts: From householders, the homeless
iti107:4.2 starts: receive requisites:
iti107:4.3 starts: robes, lodgings,
iti107:4.4 starts: protection from inclemencies.
iti111:8.1 starts: Controlled in walking,
iti111:8.2 starts: controlled in sitting,
iti111:8.3 starts: controlled in lying down,
iti111:8.4 starts: controlled in flexing & extending his limbs
iti111:10.1 starts: a monk who dwells thus ardently,
iti111:10.2 starts: not restlessly, at peace–
iti111:10.3 starts: always
iti111:10.4 starts: training in the mastery
iti111:10.5 starts: is said to be continually
iti111:10.6 starts: resolute.
